WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.465
Let's make A twig-and-leaf picture frame.

2
00:00:02.845 --> 00:00:07.130
Decorate an adult-prepared cardboard frame with twigs and leaf corners.

3
00:00:07.510 --> 00:00:09.930
The cardboard provides the structure.

4
00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:12.390
Make this project with a grown-up.

5
00:00:12.770 --> 00:00:15.500
Gather the supplies listed below the video.

6
00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:18.125
Pause whenever you need more time.

7
00:00:18.505 --> 00:00:21.935
An adult cuts the cardboard window and prepares twig lengths.

8
00:00:22.315 --> 00:00:26.637
This frame rests on a shelf or table; it is not designed to hang

9
00:00:26.637 --> 00:00:27.255
above anyone.

10
00:00:28.667 --> 00:00:29.857
Step 1.

11
00:00:30.237 --> 00:00:31.597
Choose the picture.

12
00:00:31.977 --> 00:00:36.112
Set the cardboard frame over a drawing or photograph to check the window.

13
00:00:36.492 --> 00:00:39.067
Keep the picture aside while decorating.

14
00:00:39.447 --> 00:00:42.012
Place the frame flat on the table.

15
00:00:42.392 --> 00:00:43.772
Grown-up help.

16
00:00:44.152 --> 00:00:47.132
Prepare the cardboard window and smooth edges.

17
00:00:48.667 --> 00:00:49.847
Step 2.

18
00:00:50.227 --> 00:00:52.242
Lay out four twig sides.

19
00:00:52.622 --> 00:00:55.437
Place one twig on each cardboard side.

20
00:00:55.817 --> 00:00:58.697
Keep all twig ends within the outer cardboard edge.

21
00:00:59.077 --> 00:01:01.607
Leave the corners clear enough for leaves.

22
00:01:01.987 --> 00:01:03.367
Grown-up help.

23
00:01:03.747 --> 00:01:06.437
Prepare twig lengths without child cutting.

24
00:01:07.834 --> 00:01:09.179
Step 3.

25
00:01:09.559 --> 00:01:11.144
Tape the twig border.

26
00:01:11.524 --> 00:01:15.356
At two points on each side, wrap a short strip of tape over the

27
00:01:15.356 --> 00:01:18.094
twig, around the outer cardboard edge and onto the back.

28
00:01:18.474 --> 00:01:21.059
Press firmly so the twig cannot roll.

29
00:01:21.439 --> 00:01:22.819
Grown-up help.

30
00:01:23.199 --> 00:01:25.489
Help attach and check all four twigs.

31
00:01:27.001 --> 00:01:28.151
Step 4.

32
00:01:28.531 --> 00:01:30.141
Add leaf corners.

33
00:01:30.521 --> 00:01:34.698
Make a small tape loop behind each leaf and press it onto a cardboard

34
00:01:34.698 --> 00:01:34.996
corner.

35
00:01:35.376 --> 00:01:38.496
Choose leaves that do not cover the picture window.

36
00:01:38.876 --> 00:01:40.826
Add another loop if a leaf lifts.

37
00:01:41.206 --> 00:01:42.586
Grown-up help.

38
00:01:42.966 --> 00:01:45.556
Prepare tape loops for younger makers.

39
00:01:47.001 --> 00:01:48.176
Step 5.

40
00:01:48.556 --> 00:01:49.661
Fit the artwork.

41
00:01:50.041 --> 00:01:52.071
Turn the frame over carefully.

42
00:01:52.451 --> 00:01:56.772
Centre the picture face-down over the window and tape its four edges to the

43
00:01:56.772 --> 00:01:57.081
back.

44
00:01:57.461 --> 00:02:01.216
Turn it upright and lean it against a stable wall on a low shelf.

45
00:02:01.596 --> 00:02:02.976
Grown-up help.

46
00:02:03.356 --> 00:02:06.776
Check the display is stable and out of younger children’s reach.

47
00:02:08.168 --> 00:02:11.083
Here are three ideas for your finished project.

48
00:02:11.463 --> 00:02:15.013
These example pictures were made with artificial intelligence.

49
00:02:15.393 --> 00:02:17.413
Your creation can look different.

50
00:02:17.793 --> 00:02:21.013
Remove the photograph, tape and natural pieces.

51
00:02:21.393 --> 00:02:24.093
Reuse the frame if it remains sturdy.

52
00:02:24.473 --> 00:02:28.443
Keep indoors and dry; replace leaves when they become brittle.

53
00:02:28.823 --> 00:02:29.813
Well done.

54
00:02:30.193 --> 00:02:32.623
Take a moment to enjoy what you made.

